{
  "schema": "ns3-e2-metric-map",
  "v": 1,
  "doc": [
    "Metric map v1: which ns3-e2-ipc.v1 sample value becomes which E2SM-KPM measurement.",
    "The agent loads the rows of its E2_NODE_KIND, logs the file's sha256 and advertises sha8 in ranFunction-Description ('ns-O-RAN KPM map v1 <sha8>').",
    "The M6 gate reads this same file at the pinned Testbed SHA and compares its sha with the one on the wire.",
    "Row fields:",
    "  kind: gnb | enb (the LTE eNB registers as a gNB-type E2 node, design S2).",
    "  list: cell (IndicationMessage format 1, report style 1, action format 1) | ue (format 2, style 3, action format 3).",
    "  order: 1..n position in the list; records follow this order exactly. measId: cell = order, ue = 1000 + order (stable; append-only).",
    "  kpm: KPM measName, PrintableString-legal (no '_'); one record type per name across the whole map. A 3GPP name is the clause's name (gNB rows: 3GPP TS 28.552 V20.2.0, eNB rows: 3GPP TS 32.425 V19.0.0) and only where schema/kpm-measurement-clauses.v1.json holds its clause and a value check that holds for this row's src; every other value has a vendor name ns3.<section>.<name> that reuses no 3GPP family name or placeholder. A renamed row keeps its order and measId.",
    "  type: INTEGER only for values guaranteed in 0..2^31-1 (kpimon casts to int32); everything else REAL. Out of range -> noValue + int32Overflow.",
    "  scope: sample (pointer from the sample object) | ue (pointer from one element of sample.ues).",
    "  src: JSON pointer; keys inside sections are the exact ns-3 AddItem strings, container/CSV-only values use the C++ field names.",
    "  xform: none | ns_to_ms_floor (floor(ns / 1e6)).",
    "  unit: for a 3GPP name, the registry's unit (KPM v03.00 7.9.1 where it lists the name, else the clause's; 'count' where the clause states none); for an ns3.* name, informational.",
    "  clause: '3GPP TS <spec> <version> §<clause>' of the registry entry, or 'vendor' for an ns3.* name. layer: PHY | MAC | RLC | PDCP | RRC (the src section must fit: du PHY/MAC/RLC, cuUp PDCP, cuCp RRC), or none for the ns3.* identity rows (ns3.nodeId, ns3.simTimeMs, ns3.seq, and ns3.imsi in the UE list) and only for them. An ns3.* row whose quantity ns-3 reports outside its layer's section (the RLC counters of the CU-UP reports, the RRC UE-map size of the en-gNB DU report) is named in the lint's VENDOR_LAYER_EXCEPTIONS.",
    "  origin (where ns-3 computes the value), legacyName (ns-3's previous measurement/column name) are informational.",
    "Missing or null values are encoded as noValue. Both lists start with ns3.nodeId, ns3.simTimeMs, ns3.seq; ns3.imsi is UE item 4.",
    "Join keys: cellMetrics on (ns3.nodeId, ns3.seq); UeMetrics on (ns3.nodeId, ns3.seq, ns3.imsi). Never on _time.",
    "Lint: tests/lint-metric-map.py (registry: schema/kpm-measurement-clauses.v1.json; fixtures: --self-test)."
  ],
